WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.556 --> 00:00:05.769
Welcome to Ear Biscuits, the podcast

00:00:05.769 --> 00:00:10.389
where two lifelong friends talk
about life for a long time.

00:00:10.389 --> 00:00:12.387
Sometimes a really long time.

00:00:12.387 --> 00:00:13.220
I'm Link.

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:14.403
And I'm Rhett.

00:00:14.403 --> 00:00:17.579
This week at The Round
Table Of Dim Lighting

00:00:17.579 --> 00:00:21.007
is the second part of our podcast.

00:00:21.007 --> 00:00:22.473
The conversation that we just finished.

00:00:22.473 --> 00:00:26.217
That we recorded last, that
you listened to last week,

00:00:26.217 --> 00:00:28.662
but we sat down and we recorded
it all at the same time.

00:00:28.662 --> 00:00:31.335
Basically what happened
as we indicated last week

00:00:31.335 --> 00:00:35.115
is that we were having a
conversation about board games,

00:00:35.115 --> 00:00:39.176
and I brought up my
repeated accusation of Link,

00:00:39.176 --> 00:00:42.822
which is that I feel that he
is just as competitive as me,

00:00:42.822 --> 00:00:46.322
and that opened a huge can of worms about,

00:00:47.406 --> 00:00:50.406
pooh, man, it just got, it got deep.

00:00:51.592 --> 00:00:54.342
And I don't know exactly
when Kiko is gonna decide,

00:00:54.342 --> 00:00:56.476
so what we're about to play
for you in the conversation,

00:00:56.476 --> 00:00:58.121
it might overlap a little bit,

00:00:58.121 --> 00:00:59.473
it might backtrack a little bit

00:00:59.473 --> 00:01:03.140
with where last week's ended
before we cut in, I don't know.

00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:04.942
Kiko, how you are gonna do this?

00:01:04.942 --> 00:01:09.530
But I think this is an
important conversation.

00:01:09.530 --> 00:01:13.697
And I think it will make
you feel better to know

00:01:16.383 --> 00:01:19.567
that we've had this conversation already

00:01:19.567 --> 00:01:21.068
that you're about to listen to,

00:01:21.068 --> 00:01:23.111
and everything is okay.

00:01:23.111 --> 00:01:24.091
Yeah, we're still good.

00:01:24.091 --> 00:01:29.091
We are okay, it got kind of
intense in a couple of places,

00:01:31.594 --> 00:01:35.202
but I think it was a good conversation.

00:01:35.202 --> 00:01:37.385
I'm glad that it happened.

00:01:37.385 --> 00:01:39.733
I don't know how you're
going to interpret it,

00:01:39.733 --> 00:01:42.577
but as we said at the end of last week,

00:01:42.577 --> 00:01:47.436
as you interact with this
conversation, as you listen to it,

00:01:47.436 --> 00:01:49.136
and then as you talk about it online,

00:01:49.136 --> 00:01:52.596
we would just ask that in the spirit

00:01:52.596 --> 00:01:55.265
that we tried to embody,
as we had the discussion,

00:01:55.265 --> 00:01:56.932
which is a spirit of

00:01:59.502 --> 00:02:01.336
goodwill, I would say.

00:02:01.336 --> 00:02:04.174
It's like we said some
hard things or whatever,

00:02:04.174 --> 00:02:06.757
but the whole point of this is,

00:02:07.787 --> 00:02:10.080
it's not for it to become some competition

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:12.274
between the two of us where you're like,

00:02:12.274 --> 00:02:13.592
well, I think that Rhett was right

00:02:13.592 --> 00:02:16.840
or I think that Link was right or...

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:18.507
How can we be illuminating in the way

00:02:18.507 --> 00:02:20.818
that we continue the conversation, right?

00:02:20.818 --> 00:02:21.651
How can you be illuminated?

00:02:21.651 --> 00:02:25.124
How can we all understand each other more?

00:02:25.124 --> 00:02:28.027
Yeah, and what does this make
you think about yourself?

00:02:28.027 --> 00:02:31.545
Not just what you think
about one or both of us,

00:02:31.545 --> 00:02:33.600
but like how do you relate
to some of the things

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:36.106
that we're seeing and what does
it make you think about your

00:02:36.106 --> 00:02:38.911
own personal journey and the
way that you see the world?

00:02:38.911 --> 00:02:41.635
And maybe this is, I mean,

00:02:41.635 --> 00:02:43.338
maybe this is the end of the conversation,

00:02:43.338 --> 00:02:45.734
but it's the beginning
of the conversation.

00:02:45.734 --> 00:02:47.849
And I'm not talking about this episode.

00:02:47.849 --> 00:02:50.007
I don't know, I'm just,

00:02:50.007 --> 00:02:52.507
I don't know how much it like.

00:02:53.359 --> 00:02:55.433
I mean, I-
I just wanna talk about it.

00:02:55.433 --> 00:02:58.576
We made it sound like this is crazy.

00:02:58.576 --> 00:02:59.659
Yeah, I don't think it's crazy.

00:02:59.659 --> 00:03:00.521
We built it up too much.

00:03:00.521 --> 00:03:01.354
Yeah, we built it up.

00:03:01.354 --> 00:03:03.212
It's just a conversation about board games

00:03:03.212 --> 00:03:05.162
became a conversation about our friendship

00:03:05.162 --> 00:03:06.995
and the way that we view

00:03:06.995 --> 00:03:09.636
the interplay between the two of us.

00:03:09.636 --> 00:03:11.051
Well, just, and here it is,

00:03:11.051 --> 00:03:13.039
and now you can listen to it.

00:03:13.039 --> 00:03:13.872
Here it is.

00:03:17.521 --> 00:03:19.800
Ultimately everybody wants to be

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:21.352
important in some way, right.

00:03:21.352 --> 00:03:25.274
And people who are in
entertainment kind of achieve that

00:03:25.274 --> 00:03:29.233
and find their purpose a lot of times in,

00:03:29.233 --> 00:03:31.310
eliciting a reaction from people.

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:35.893
And I would say that you are
actually even more focused

00:03:38.182 --> 00:03:41.567
and committed to getting
a reaction from a crowd

00:03:41.567 --> 00:03:44.458
or from a individual than I am.

00:03:44.458 --> 00:03:46.682
You think about like
the way that your super,

00:03:46.682 --> 00:03:50.894
I'm much less concerned about things like,

00:03:50.894 --> 00:03:53.302
where is this thing and
where is the camera,

00:03:53.302 --> 00:03:54.150
and I'm not showing,

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:56.868
I'm not opening this box in the right way.

00:03:56.868 --> 00:03:59.697
In my mind, that's all competitive nature.

00:03:59.697 --> 00:04:03.394
It's like you have a
commitment to excellence,

00:04:03.394 --> 00:04:06.645
and you're thinking about
competitiveness in like,

00:04:06.645 --> 00:04:10.505
I'm throwing a ball faster
than a person or not,

00:04:10.505 --> 00:04:14.264
but you actually care about
that stuff more than I do.

00:04:14.264 --> 00:04:16.764
And I would call that sort of,

00:04:18.469 --> 00:04:21.793
I would almost say it's
a relentless pursuit

00:04:21.793 --> 00:04:23.880
of doing things in a certain way.

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:27.190
Perfection is not, I mean-
I interpret that as-

00:04:27.190 --> 00:04:31.107
Is attained by comparison
to like a standard.

00:04:33.351 --> 00:04:34.184
Yes.

00:04:34.184 --> 00:04:36.615
But I think it's a stretch to
say that that's competition,

00:04:36.615 --> 00:04:39.948
like I'm competing against the standard.

00:04:40.855 --> 00:04:42.250
Now I also think this is,

00:04:42.250 --> 00:04:45.000
I think it's a little muddied by,

00:04:46.183 --> 00:04:47.641
I don't know.

00:04:47.641 --> 00:04:52.131
Do you get from me in
this conversation that

00:04:52.131 --> 00:04:54.240
like I judge you for being competitive?

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:55.073
Yes.

00:04:55.073 --> 00:04:58.722
That, and I think, that's interesting

00:04:58.722 --> 00:05:00.824
because I think that's
really what's going on

00:05:00.824 --> 00:05:04.491
is that your counterpoint
is you feel judged

00:05:06.018 --> 00:05:07.766
by me for being competitive.

00:05:07.766 --> 00:05:08.599
I think what-

00:05:08.599 --> 00:05:09.695
And so then you're trying to put it on me.

00:05:09.695 --> 00:05:11.286
And I hear you say is that like-

00:05:11.286 --> 00:05:12.918
Hey man, I just don't.

00:05:12.918 --> 00:05:14.149
I am superior-
I don't.

00:05:14.149 --> 00:05:15.173
Because I'm not competitive.

00:05:15.173 --> 00:05:17.001
I don't bother with like wanting to win

00:05:17.001 --> 00:05:19.711
a stupid game for
somebody, that's kind of-

00:05:19.711 --> 00:05:22.408
But I don't believe that,
I don't believe that.

00:05:22.408 --> 00:05:27.408
I think you're, I just, I
don't think that's happening.

00:05:27.474 --> 00:05:30.246
And I guess, and what I'm saying,

00:05:30.246 --> 00:05:32.167
so that's part of it, but I also what I'm,

00:05:32.167 --> 00:05:33.590
one of the things I'm saying is that

00:05:33.590 --> 00:05:36.007
I feel like our entire career

00:05:38.533 --> 00:05:41.616
is based on a competition ultimately.

00:05:43.737 --> 00:05:48.037
I think there's a
competition against ourselves

00:05:48.037 --> 00:05:50.599
and against our like,
looking back on something

00:05:50.599 --> 00:05:53.383
that we did and not liking
it and wanting to do better.

00:05:53.383 --> 00:05:55.665
Well, but seeing that as a competition is

00:05:55.665 --> 00:05:58.176
because you're a competitive person.

00:05:58.176 --> 00:05:59.526
I just don't,

00:05:59.526 --> 00:06:01.966
like we're not competing
against ourselves trying to-

00:06:01.966 --> 00:06:04.722
But we're also constantly
competing against each other.

00:06:04.722 --> 00:06:06.539
So you're saying like-
That's part of it as well.

00:06:06.539 --> 00:06:09.372
It's like, you think about the way

00:06:10.658 --> 00:06:13.088
me and you like to divide
everything up like,

00:06:13.088 --> 00:06:15.474
so, all right, we're
gonna do this meeting,

00:06:15.474 --> 00:06:17.056
so you're gonna say these things

00:06:17.056 --> 00:06:18.154
and I'm gonna say these things,

00:06:18.154 --> 00:06:20.038
don't say more than me,

00:06:20.038 --> 00:06:22.589
and we're both equally committed to that.

00:06:22.589 --> 00:06:24.697
And so if you think.

00:06:24.697 --> 00:06:27.261
I just don't think I view
that as a competition, but-

00:06:27.261 --> 00:06:29.298
But what is it if it's not a competition?

00:06:29.298 --> 00:06:30.917
It's something that I care about deeply,

00:06:30.917 --> 00:06:32.422
that's a different thing that,

00:06:32.422 --> 00:06:36.232
again, I'm not judging you if
you see it as a competition.

00:06:36.232 --> 00:06:37.226
Well, if it's not a competition-

00:06:37.226 --> 00:06:38.889
But I don't, but that's just the,

00:06:38.889 --> 00:06:41.720
that's the way you look at the world.

00:06:41.720 --> 00:06:44.548
And when you see me act
in the way that you would,

00:06:44.548 --> 00:06:45.828
again, I think it's something different,

00:06:45.828 --> 00:06:50.828
like me being a perfectionist
to a flawed point, absolutely.

00:06:51.448 --> 00:06:55.448
Like I could be defensive
about like, yeah, I'm,

00:06:56.398 --> 00:06:59.174
I think about how I open
boxes like whatever you are,

00:06:59.174 --> 00:07:00.536
I know exactly what you're talking about.

00:07:00.536 --> 00:07:02.926
Well, I'm saying that I think that that,

00:07:02.926 --> 00:07:05.182
and I don't think that's
a bad thing ultimately

00:07:05.182 --> 00:07:06.015
is what I'm saying.

00:07:06.015 --> 00:07:09.440
I think that that is a sign of someone.

00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:13.112
But I'm saying there are things about me,

00:07:13.112 --> 00:07:15.621
like I'm a perfectionist,
just like you could say,

00:07:15.621 --> 00:07:17.010
I'm a competitive person.

00:07:17.010 --> 00:07:18.686
Let's just, and I'm saying,

00:07:18.686 --> 00:07:20.803
well, there were flaws
associated with that,

00:07:20.803 --> 00:07:22.515
but I'm not putting that on,

00:07:22.515 --> 00:07:24.424
I'm not judging you being competitive.

00:07:24.424 --> 00:07:29.025
I'm saying the only thing,
I guess I was insinuating

00:07:29.025 --> 00:07:32.837
was sometimes when you're not competitive

00:07:32.837 --> 00:07:34.490
and you're around competitive people,

00:07:34.490 --> 00:07:37.240
it doesn't, it's not a good time,

00:07:38.153 --> 00:07:40.986
but that's not a judgment on that,

00:07:42.388 --> 00:07:44.146
because you're a bad person.

00:07:44.146 --> 00:07:46.559
Yeah, I think what I am saying is,

00:07:46.559 --> 00:07:49.476
I mean, I think that is part of it,

00:07:50.777 --> 00:07:52.138
but I think what I'm saying is that

00:07:52.138 --> 00:07:56.608
my understanding of the
competitive spirit is something

00:07:56.608 --> 00:08:00.714
that I think that there are
elements of your personality

00:08:00.714 --> 00:08:03.888
that are based in a competitive spirit.

00:08:03.888 --> 00:08:05.374
Yes, that's true.

00:08:05.374 --> 00:08:09.002
And much more than you
give yourself credit for it

00:08:09.002 --> 00:08:13.412
because I don't think it's
a bad thing, right, because,

00:08:13.412 --> 00:08:16.479
and whether you want to
use the term 'competitive'

00:08:16.479 --> 00:08:18.729
or not, but it's just like,

00:08:20.083 --> 00:08:22.082
and I think that the competition,

00:08:22.082 --> 00:08:25.415
and I don't mean the staged competition,

00:08:26.823 --> 00:08:29.507
but in every relationship, every marriage,

00:08:29.507 --> 00:08:33.918
every creative partnership,
there is healthy competition.

00:08:33.918 --> 00:08:35.867
If there is not healthy competition,

00:08:35.867 --> 00:08:38.089
then it's just one person
just doing everything

00:08:38.089 --> 00:08:40.237
and getting their way, but that isn't,

00:08:40.237 --> 00:08:42.308
that isn't the nature of our partnership.

00:08:42.308 --> 00:08:45.539
It's just like I fight for
ideas, you fight for ideas.

00:08:45.539 --> 00:08:47.110
You have things that are important to you,

00:08:47.110 --> 00:08:49.163
I have things that are important to me,

00:08:49.163 --> 00:08:51.467
and we fight for those things, right.

00:08:51.467 --> 00:08:53.800
And the creative process is,

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:58.380
is based in a competitive spirit, I think.

00:09:00.793 --> 00:09:01.626
For you.

00:09:01.626 --> 00:09:06.043
I think for me, I want things
just as badly as you do

00:09:08.523 --> 00:09:11.606
and for good reasons and bad reasons,

00:09:12.488 --> 00:09:15.071
but I just don't, I don't look,

00:09:16.132 --> 00:09:18.744
I don't look at that through
a lens of competition

00:09:18.744 --> 00:09:21.062
as readily as you do.

00:09:21.062 --> 00:09:23.784
And I look through a different lens

00:09:23.784 --> 00:09:26.996
depending on what the example is.

00:09:26.996 --> 00:09:30.715
And I just think that's how
we see things differently

00:09:30.715 --> 00:09:32.695
and things resonate with us differently.

00:09:32.695 --> 00:09:35.293
Like the more something
is overtly competition,

00:09:35.293 --> 00:09:37.467
the more I am going to shrink from it,

00:09:37.467 --> 00:09:40.427
and the more you are
going to engage with it.

00:09:40.427 --> 00:09:43.247
I think that's the definition.

00:09:43.247 --> 00:09:46.575
To me that's the definition
of, are you competitive person?

00:09:46.575 --> 00:09:50.149
When you're faced with some
of this obviously competitive,

00:09:50.149 --> 00:09:51.732
how do you respond?

00:09:53.872 --> 00:09:57.705
And, again, with no
judgment attached to that.

00:09:59.681 --> 00:10:00.917
Yeah, I get that.

00:10:00.917 --> 00:10:03.109
Yeah, I think it's very simply that

00:10:03.109 --> 00:10:04.955
I see it as broader than that.

00:10:04.955 --> 00:10:06.826
Like I think that even

00:10:06.826 --> 00:10:08.201
like we talked about this for years,

00:10:08.201 --> 00:10:11.034
like when we, when me and you are,

00:10:13.023 --> 00:10:16.889
like when we're performing,
it's just like, are you tell...

00:10:16.889 --> 00:10:21.889
I refuse to believe that there
is not something in your mind

00:10:22.090 --> 00:10:24.654
because we've talked
about it a million times.

00:10:24.654 --> 00:10:26.753
Like if we're watching
an edit of something

00:10:26.753 --> 00:10:29.165
that is more like, we
went out and did something

00:10:29.165 --> 00:10:30.404
and now we're editing it.

00:10:30.404 --> 00:10:33.051
Sure, we balance.
We wanna balance,

00:10:33.051 --> 00:10:36.068
but we were not trying
to achieve that balance

00:10:36.068 --> 00:10:38.235
just in the name of brand.

00:10:39.235 --> 00:10:41.792
It's just like, I'm fully ready.

00:10:41.792 --> 00:10:44.930
I'm fully willing to
admit that it's just like,

00:10:44.930 --> 00:10:47.284
I want to be able to watch that video

00:10:47.284 --> 00:10:51.243
and think I contributed to
the comedy in this video,

00:10:51.243 --> 00:10:53.340
like I got some good lines in there.

00:10:53.340 --> 00:10:54.855
And if I watch a video, I'm like,

00:10:54.855 --> 00:10:58.968
man, I didn't really get to
express myself in the way

00:10:58.968 --> 00:11:00.615
that I would like to.

00:11:00.615 --> 00:11:02.696
If I could go back and
engineer this video,

00:11:02.696 --> 00:11:06.424
it would be like a 50:50
thing whereas you know what,

00:11:06.424 --> 00:11:09.368
Link got a bunch of good one
liners in there in this video,

00:11:09.368 --> 00:11:13.285
and now, so for me, I'm
saying that there is a,

00:11:14.529 --> 00:11:17.328
what I think is ultimately
a healthy competition.

00:11:17.328 --> 00:11:20.624
It's not like, oh, I want
to get more than Link.

00:11:20.624 --> 00:11:22.070
I don't want Link to say anything funny

00:11:22.070 --> 00:11:22.903
because that would be like.

00:11:22.903 --> 00:11:24.722
Yeah, I just don't call that competition.

00:11:24.722 --> 00:11:27.369
So what is it if it's not?

00:11:27.369 --> 00:11:30.202
Because I would think if you could,

00:11:30.202 --> 00:11:31.869
I don't view that as comp.

00:11:31.869 --> 00:11:35.040
First of all, we agree
in what we're after.

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:37.851
Like we talk about balance a lot,

00:11:37.851 --> 00:11:41.373
but the way that I
think, like I just don't,

00:11:41.373 --> 00:11:43.579
I don't think I think about
it in terms of competition.

00:11:43.579 --> 00:11:45.866
I think about it in terms of pulling,

00:11:45.866 --> 00:11:47.634
pulling my weight or contributing.

00:11:47.634 --> 00:11:49.770
What I'm saying is personal though.

00:11:49.770 --> 00:11:52.024
I think ultimately I'm saying is that,

00:11:52.024 --> 00:11:53.956
it is personally motivated.

00:11:53.956 --> 00:11:56.353
It isn't like I'm trying to meet,

00:11:56.353 --> 00:11:59.463
it's not like you're
trying to meet an external

00:11:59.463 --> 00:12:04.463
quota of like, we've decided
in some times long past

00:12:04.601 --> 00:12:08.421
that we are 50:50 contributing
to as much as possible,

00:12:08.421 --> 00:12:11.668
but it's like in the moment
when you're watching a video

00:12:11.668 --> 00:12:14.698
and you're like, I'm trying to get,

00:12:14.698 --> 00:12:17.720
I want to be an equal partner in this,

00:12:17.720 --> 00:12:22.630
I think there's an element of
competition that's based on

00:12:22.630 --> 00:12:25.277
you're an advocate for yourself

00:12:25.277 --> 00:12:27.860
in a non-prideful, healthy way.

00:12:29.608 --> 00:12:32.507
In other words, like if I were to go in

00:12:32.507 --> 00:12:35.654
and edit a video without you being there

00:12:35.654 --> 00:12:37.774
and you were like, man, I
said a bunch of funny things

00:12:37.774 --> 00:12:41.017
and he's edited those things
out when I wasn't there.

00:12:41.017 --> 00:12:42.329
You would be...

00:12:42.329 --> 00:12:44.193
Would you be personally offended?

00:12:44.193 --> 00:12:46.286
And would you be offended

00:12:46.286 --> 00:12:48.700
because we're not meeting some standard

00:12:48.700 --> 00:12:49.785
